#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1367 expect=skipped domain=DS
#note "EPOCH column absent: rows 1/2 duplicate (USUBJID, DSSCAT) disposition events, but the rule's EPOCH gate stops it instead of letting it run the coarser per-DSSCAT check. WHY skipped AND NOT noViolation (wave-17 lane A, R-4.11 hoist): the gate used to be a top-level 'EPOCH exists' leaf and this fixture then asserted expect=noViolation - the rule executed to a silent zero. It is now Requirements.Variables.All EPOCH, so the same zero is reported as 'skipped - variable EPOCH absent'. Violations are 0 both ways; only the reporting changed. ⚠ The superseded note here called this the 'endorsed Check-exists shape ... needs the Perm comparator present': EPOCH is the is_not_unique_set TARGET, not a comparator, and R-4.11a was re-scoped to a POSITION rule on 2026-08-07 that reaches the grouping key only. DSSCAT keeps BOTH halves because it IS a grouping key."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DS class=EVENTS
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSCAT   type=Char label="Category for Disposition Event"
col DSSCAT  type=Char label="Subcategory for Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | S1-001 | 1 | ADVERSE EVENT | ADVERSE EVENT | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY TREATMENT
S1 | DS | S1-001 | 2 | COMPLETED     | COMPLETED     | DISPOSITION EVENT | STUDY TREATMENT
